ese tools have matured to the point where they reduce the capture fragility risk materially.\n\n**Market size and willingness to pay.** No output has access to buyer research, pricing benchmarks for adjacent tools, or evidence of budget allocation for demo-generation workflows. The claim that this is a \"budget-worthy\" pain is unverified in all three outputs.\n\n**Whether Supademo, Arcade, or Storylane expose APIs sufficient for programmatic demo creation.** Model 2 raises this as a strategic question but cannot answer it. If yes, the build-vs-integrate calculus shifts significantly.\n\n**Interview completion rates in practice.** The 60% completion threshold proposed by Models 2 and 3 is a reasonable hypothesis, but no empirical data on engineer compliance with merge-time prompts (beyond PR description completion rates as a rough proxy) is available in any of the three outputs.\n\n**Whether the pre-fill quality is achievable.** Model 2 proposes an experiment (blind-rate 30 pre-filled interviews for hallucination rate, kill if >15% confident-wrong) but the baseline hallucination rate for this specific task on current LLMs is not established in any output."
